## Exercise

Build a “Create Todo” feature in TypeScript using **layered architecture**.

**Requirements**
- Create a todo with a `title` (required) and optional `description`.
- `title` must be non-empty and at most 100 characters; otherwise throw a domain validation error.
- Persist todos in an in-memory repository.
- Expose a function/use-case `createTodo(input)` that returns the created todo with `id` and `createdAt`.
- Keep layers separate:
  1. **Domain**: `Todo` entity + validation + repository interface.
  2. **Application**: `CreateTodoUseCase`.
  3. **Infrastructure**: `InMemoryTodoRepository`.
  4. **Presentation**: a small CLI adapter calling the use case.

Dependencies must point inward: outer layers depend on inner layers, never the reverse.

---

## Step-by-step solution

### 1. Define the domain layer

The domain owns the business rules and the repository contract. It has no dependencies on frameworks, storage, or presentation.

```ts
// src/domain/Todo.ts
export interface Todo {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly title: string;
  readonly description?: string;
  readonly createdAt: Date;
}

export class TodoValidationError extends Error {
  constructor(message: string) {
    super(message);
    this.name = "TodoValidationError";
  }
}

export function createTodoEntity(
  id: string,
  title: string,
  description: string | undefined,
  createdAt: Date
): Todo {
  const trimmedTitle = title.trim();

  if (trimmedTitle.length === 0) {
    throw new TodoValidationError("Title must not be empty.");
  }

  if (trimmedTitle.length > 100) {
    throw new TodoValidationError("Title must be at most 100 characters.");
  }

  return {
    id,
    title: trimmedTitle,
    description: description?.trim() || undefined,
    createdAt,
  };
}
```

```ts
// src/domain/TodoRepository.ts
import type { Todo } from "./Todo";

export interface TodoRepository {
  save(todo: Todo): Promise<Todo>;
  findAll(): Promise<readonly Todo[]>;
}
```

### 2. Define the application layer

The use case coordinates the domain and infrastructure, but only depends on abstractions.

```ts
// src/application/CreateTodoUseCase.ts
import type { Todo, TodoValidationError } from "../domain/Todo";
import type { TodoRepository } from "../domain/TodoRepository";

export interface CreateTodoInput {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
}

export class CreateTodoUseCase {
  constructor(
    private readonly repository: TodoRepository,
    private readonly idGenerator: () => string,
    private readonly clock: () => Date
  ) {}

  async execute(input: CreateTodoInput): Promise<Todo> {
    const todo = createTodoEntity(
      this.idGenerator(),
      input.title,
      input.description,
      this.clock()
    );

    return this.repository.save(todo);
  }
}
```

Note: `createTodoEntity` is imported from the domain, so validation remains in the domain layer.

### 3. Implement the infrastructure layer

This is the only place that knows about in-memory storage.

```ts
// src/infrastructure/InMemoryTodoRepository.ts
import type { Todo } from "../domain/Todo";
import type { TodoRepository } from "../domain/TodoRepository";

export class InMemoryTodoRepository implements TodoRepository {
  private readonly todos = new Map<string, Todo>();

  async save(todo: Todo): Promise<Todo> {
    this.todos.set(todo.id, todo);
    return todo;
  }

  async findAll(): Promise<readonly Todo[]> {
    return [...this.todos.values()];
  }
}
```

### 4. Add the presentation layer

A thin adapter translates external input into use-case calls.

```ts
// src/presentation/cli.ts
import { CreateTodoUseCase } from "../application/CreateTodoUseCase";
import { InMemoryTodoRepository } from "../infrastructure/InMemoryTodoRepository";

export async function runCli(args: string[]): Promise<void> {
  const repository = new InMemoryTodoRepository();

  const useCase = new CreateTodoUseCase(
    repository,
    () => crypto.randomUUID(),
    () => new Date()
  );

  const title = args[0] ?? "";
  const description = args[1];

  try {
    const todo = await useCase.execute({ title, description });
    console.log("Created todo:", todo);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error instanceof Error) {
      console.error("Failed:", error.message);
    } else {
      console.error("Failed: unknown error");
    }
  }
}
```

### 5. Composition root

Wire dependencies in one place, usually at application startup.

```ts
// src/index.ts
import { runCli } from "./presentation/cli";

runCli(process.argv.slice(2));
```

