## Why this shape matters (interview talking points)

- **Domain purity:** `User` and `UserRepository` have zero imports from outer layers → unit-testable with no DB/HTTP.
- **Ports & adapters:** swapping `InMemoryUserRepository` for a Postgres repo changes only infrastructure + composition root; use case & controller unchanged.
- **Error modeling:** domain/application throw typed errors; presentation maps them to HTTP statuses (no HTTP concepts leak inward).
- **Validation split:** input shape validation at boundary (controller) vs. business invariants in entity/use case.
- **Testing:** mock `UserRepository` to test `RegisterUserUseCase` in isolation; test controller with a fake use case.

