Below are common edge cases when applying layered architecture in TypeScript (Presentation → Application/Service → Domain → Infrastructure). Each section shows an anti-pattern or risk and an idiomatic fix.

---

## 1. Circular dependencies between layers/services

**Risk:** `OrderService` imports `InventoryService`, which imports `OrderService` → build/runtime cycles and hidden coupling.

**Fix:** depend on ports (interfaces) defined in the application/domain layer; wire implementations in infrastructure/composition root.

```ts
// application/ports/InventoryPort.ts
export interface InventoryPort {
  reserve(sku: string, qty: number): Promise<void>;
}

// application/OrderService.ts
export class OrderService {
  constructor(
    private readonly inventory: InventoryPort,
    private readonly orders: OrderRepository,
  ) {}

  async placeOrder(input: PlaceOrderInput): Promise<OrderDto> {
    await this.inventory.reserve(input.sku, input.qty);
    const order = Order.create(input);
    await this.orders.save(order);
    return OrderMapper.toDto(order);
  }
}

// infrastructure/InventoryAdapter.ts
export class InventoryAdapter implements InventoryPort {
  async reserve(sku: string, qty: number) {
    // DB/HTTP call
  }
}
```

---

## 2. Domain model leaking across boundaries

**Risk:** Controllers return ORM entities or domain objects with secrets (password hashes, internal flags).

**Fix:** map to DTOs at the application boundary; keep domain entities inside.

```ts
// domain/User.ts
export class User {
  constructor(
    public readonly id: string,
    public readonly email: Email,
    private readonly passwordHash: string,
  ) {}

  toPublic(): UserPublic {
    return { id: this.id, email: this.email.value };
  }
}

// application/dto/UserDto.ts
export interface UserDto {
  id: string;
  email: string;
}

// application/mappers/UserMapper.ts
export const UserMapper = {
  toDto(u: User): UserDto {
    return u.toPublic();
  },
};

// presentation/UserController.ts
const dto = UserMapper.toDto(user);
res.json(dto); // never res.json(user)
```

---

## 3. Transaction boundaries spanning multiple repositories

**Risk:** Save order succeeds, inventory decrement fails → partial state.

**Fix:** use a Unit of Work / transaction context passed to repositories.

```ts
export interface TxContext { /* connection/transaction handle */ }

export interface UnitOfWork {
  run<T>(fn: (tx: TxContext) => Promise<T>): Promise<T>;
}

export interface OrderRepository {
  save(order: Order, tx: TxContext): Promise<void>;
}

export interface InventoryRepository {
  decrement(sku: string, qty: number, tx: TxContext): Promise<void>;
}

export class CheckoutService {
  constructor(private uow: UnitOfWork, private orders: OrderRepository, private inv: InventoryRepository) {}

  async checkout(input: CheckoutInput) {
    return this.uow.run(async (tx) => {
      const order = Order.create(input);
      await this.orders.save(order, tx);
      await this.inv.decrement(input.sku, input.qty, tx);
      return OrderMapper.toDto(order);
    });
  }
}
```

---

## 4. Validation placed in only one layer

**Risk:** UI validation bypassed by API clients; DB constraints surface as 500s.

**Fix:** validate shape at presentation, enforce invariants in domain, keep DB constraints as last resort.

```ts
// presentation: zod for transport shape
const CreateOrderSchema = z.object({
  sku: z.string().min(1),
  qty: z.number().int().positive(),
});

// domain: invariant
export class Quantity {
  private constructor(public readonly value: number) {}
  static of(n: number) {
    if (!Number.isInteger(n) || n <= 0) throw new DomainError('invalid quantity');
    return new Quantity(n);
  }
}

// application
export class OrderService {
  async create(raw: unknown) {
    const input = CreateOrderSchema.parse(raw); // throws ZodError -> map to 400
    const qty = Quantity.of(input.qty); // domain guard
    // ...
  }
}
```

---

## 5. Error taxonomy not translated across layers

**Risk:** Prisma/DB errors leak to clients; inconsistent HTTP status codes.

**Fix:** define domain/application errors; translate in infrastructure and presentation.

```ts
// domain/errors.ts
export class DomainError extends Error {}
export class NotFoundError extends DomainError {}
export class ConcurrencyError extends DomainError {}

// infrastructure/OrderRepositoryImpl.ts
async findById(id: string, tx?: TxContext) {
  try {
    return await prisma.order.findUniqueOrThrow({ where: { id } });
  } catch (e) {
    if (isPrismaNotFound(e)) throw new NotFoundError(`order ${id}`);
    throw e;
  }
}

// presentation/errorHandler.ts
export function toHttp(err: unknown): { status: number; body: any } {
  if (err instanceof NotFoundError) return { status: 404, body: { message: err.message } };
  if (err instanceof DomainError) return { status: 400, body: { message: err.message } };
  return { status: 500, body: { message: 'internal error' } };
}
```

---

## 6. Concurrency / lost updates

**Risk:** Two requests update same aggregate; last write wins.

**Fix:** optimistic locking with a version column; repository checks affected rows.

```ts
// domain/Order.ts
export class Order {
  constructor(public id: string, public status: OrderStatus, public version: number) {}
  cancel() {
    if (this.status !== 'placed') throw new DomainError('cannot cancel');
    this.status = 'cancelled';
  }
}

// infrastructure
async save(order: Order, tx: TxContext) {
  const res = await prisma.order.updateMany({
    where: { id: order.id, version: order.version },
    data: { status: order.status, version: { increment: 1 } },
  });
  if (res.count === 0) throw new ConcurrencyError('order changed concurrently');
}
```

---

## 7. Serialization mismatches at boundaries (Date, BigInt, Decimal)

**Risk:** `Date` becomes string over JSON unexpectedly; BigInt throws `TypeError`.

**Fix:** serialize explicitly in DTOs/mappers; parse at ingress.

```ts
// application/dto/OrderDto.ts
export interface OrderDto {
  id: string;
  createdAt: string; // ISO
  totalCents: string; // BigInt-safe
}

// mapper
export const OrderMapper = {
  toDto(o: Order): OrderDto {
    return {
      id: o.id,
      createdAt: o.createdAt.toISOString(),
      totalCents: o.totalCents.toString(),
    };
  },
};

// ingress
const input = { createdAt: new Date(body.createdAt) };
```

---

## 8. Fire-and-forget async work

**Risk:** `void sendEmail()` loses errors; unhandled rejections crash process.

**Fix:** await in transaction/outbox, or explicitly handle with logging; never ignore.

```ts
// bad
this.mailer.send(order.email); // floating promise

// better: outbox pattern
await this.uow.run(async (tx) => {
  await this.orders.save(order, tx);
  await this.outbox.enqueue({ type: 'OrderPlaced', payload: OrderMapper.toDto(order) }, tx);
});

// worker later processes outbox with retries
```

If truly best-effort:

```ts
this.audit.log(event).catch((e) => logger.error({ e }, 'audit failed'));
```

---

## 9. ORM lazy loading leaking into service/domain

**Risk:** Service accesses `order.items` triggering N+1 or DB calls outside transaction.

**Fix:** repository returns fully loaded aggregates; service works on in-memory objects only.

```ts
// repository interface (application layer)
export interface OrderRepository {
  findByIdWithItems(id: string, tx?: TxContext): Promise<Order | null>;
}

// service never touches ORM
const order = await this.orders.findByIdWithItems(id);
if (!order) throw new NotFoundError('order');
order.cancel(); // pure domain
await this.orders.save(order, tx);
```

---

## 10. Partial updates (PATCH) and invalid state transitions

**Risk:** Blindly spreading partial DTO onto entity bypasses invariants.

**Fix:** explicit patch method on aggregate with transition rules.

```ts
// application/dto/PatchOrderDto.ts
export interface PatchOrderDto {
  status?: 'cancelled' | 'shipped';
  note?: string;
}

// domain
export class Order {
  applyPatch(patch: PatchOrderDto) {
    if (patch.status === 'cancelled') this.cancel(); // validates
    if (patch.status === 'shipped') this.ship();
    if (patch.note !== undefined) this.note = patch.note.trim();
  }
}

// service
async patch(id: string, patch: PatchOrderDto) {
  const order = await this.orders.findById(id);
  if (!order) throw new NotFoundError('order');
  order.applyPatch(patch);
  await this.orders.save(order);
}
```

---

## 11. Authorization enforced only in presentation

**Risk:** Internal callers/services bypass UI checks.

**Fix:** enforce authorization in application/domain using a policy/context.

```ts
export interface Actor { id: string; roles: string[]; can(action: string, resource: unknown): boolean; }

export class OrderService {
  async cancel(orderId: string, actor: Actor) {
    const order = await this.orders.findById(orderId);
    if (!order) throw new NotFoundError('order');
    if (!actor.can('order:cancel', order)) throw new ForbiddenError();
    order.cancel();
    await this.orders.save(order);
  }
}
```

