## Typical use cases

### (a) 2D/3D graphics transforms
```ts
function rotateZ(theta: number): Mat3 {
  const c = Math.cos(theta), s = Math.sin(theta);
  return [
    [c, -s, 0],
    [s,  c, 0],
    [0,  0, 1],
  ];
}
// apply to a point: multiply matrix by column vector
```

### (b) Machine-learning feature matrices
```ts
const features: Matrix = [
  [1, 2.5, 0],
  [1, 3.1, 1],
  [1, 1.8, 0], // bias column + features
];
const weights: number[] = [0.5, 1.2, -0.3];
const preds = features.map(row =>
  row.reduce((s, x, i) => s + x * weights[i], 0)
);
```

### (c) Image convolution (kernels)
```ts
const sobelX: Matrix = [[-1, 0, 1], [-2, 0, 2], [-1, 0, 1]];
```

### (d) Solving linear systems (small N)
```ts
function det2(m: [[number, number],[number, number]]): number {
  return m[0][0] * m[1][1] - m[0][1] * m[1][0];
}
```

