## 4. Typical use cases

| Use case | Why workers help |
|---|---|
| Image/video processing | Pixel loops block the main thread |
| Large JSON parsing / transform | CPU-heavy, keeps UI responsive |
| Cryptography / hashing | Long synchronous computation |
| Physics / game simulation | Fixed-timestep updates |
| Data compression (gzip, etc.) | Heavy CPU work |
| ML inference (WASM/ONNX) | Sustained compute |
| Background indexing / search | Avoid jank |

**Not a good fit**
- I/O (network, DB, file reads): use async/await.
- Tiny tasks: worker spawn overhead dominates.
- Frequent small messages: serialization cost.

