# TypeScript Naming Conventions — Complete Runnable Example

Below is a single, self-contained file that demonstrates the most widely accepted TypeScript naming conventions (derived from the TypeScript handbook, Google style guide, and community consensus). You can run it with `npx ts-node naming.ts` or `bun naming.ts`.

## `naming.ts`

```ts
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. FILE / MODULE NAMES
//    • kebab-case for file names: user-profile.service.ts
//    • One concept per file when possible.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 2. CONSTANTS
//    • UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for true constants (compile-time / immutable values).
//    • Prefer `as const` for readonly literal objects.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const MAX_RETRY_COUNT = 3;
const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000;

const HTTP_STATUS = {
  OK: 200,
  NOT_FOUND: 404,
  SERVER_ERROR: 500,
} as const;

type HttpStatus = (typeof HTTP_STATUS)[keyof typeof HTTP_STATUS];

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 3. TYPES / INTERFACES / CLASSES / ENUMS / NAMESPACES
//    • PascalCase for all type-level identifiers.
//    • Interface: prefer `I` prefix ONLY if your team's style requires it.
//      Modern TS style usually omits it.
//    • Type aliases: PascalCase, often suffixed with context (Dto, Props, etc.)
//    • Enums: PascalCase name, UPPER_SNAKE or PascalCase members (pick one;
//      here we use UPPER_SNAKE for enum members to distinguish from TS union).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
enum UserRole {
  ADMIN = "admin",
  MEMBER = "member",
  GUEST = "guest",
}

interface User {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  role: UserRole;
  createdAt: Date;
}

type UserDto = Pick<User, "id" | "email" | "role">;
type CreateUserInput = Omit<User, "id" | "createdAt">;

class UserRepository {
  private readonly storage = new Map<string, User>();

  public async findById(id: string): Promise<User | undefined> {
    return this.storage.get(id);
  }

  public async save(user: User): Promise<void> {
    this.storage.set(user.id, user);
  }
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 4. VARIABLES / PROPERTIES / FUNCTION PARAMETERS
//    • camelCase.
//    • Booleans: prefix with is/has/can/should (isAuthenticated, hasPermission).
//    • Collections: plural nouns (users, userIds).
//    • Avoid Hungarian notation (no strName, arrItems).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const userRepository = new UserRepository();

let isAuthenticated = false;
const userPermissions = new Set<string>();

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 5. FUNCTIONS / METHODS
//    • camelCase verbs: getUserById, calculateTax.
//    • Pure predicates often prefixed with is/has/can.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
async function getUserById(id: string): Promise<User | undefined> {
  return userRepository.findById(id);
}

function isAdult(age: number): boolean {
  return age >= 18;
}

function formatCurrency(amount: number, currencyCode: string): string {
  return new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", {
    style: "currency",
    currency: currencyCode,
  }).format(amount);
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 6. REACT / UI (illustrative — kept in same file for completeness)
//    • Components: PascalCase.
//    • Props types: ComponentNameProps.
//    • Hooks: useX (camelCase starting with "use").
//    • Event handlers: handleX / onX (handleClick, onClick prop).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type ButtonProps = {
  label: string;
  onClick: () => void;
  isDisabled?: boolean;
};

function SubmitButton(props: ButtonProps): string {
  // (Returning string for a runnable, non-JSX demo.)
  return `<button ${props.isDisabled ? "disabled" : ""}>${props.label}</button>`;
}

function useCounter(initial: number): { value: number; increment: () => void } {
  let value = initial;
  return {
    value,
    increment: () => {
      value += 1;
    },
  };
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 7. GENERICS
//    • Single uppercase letter (T, K, V) for simple cases.
//    • Descriptive PascalCase for complex/meaningful params (TItem, TResult).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function mapArray<TInput, TOutput>(
  items: TInput[],
  projector: (item: TInput) => TOutput,
): TOutput[] {
  return items.map(projector);
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 8. PRIVATE / PROTECTED MEMBERS
//    • Use `#` (native private fields) or `private` keyword.
//    • Underscore prefix (_name) is legacy; prefer language features.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
class Counter {
  #value = 0; // truly private

  public get value(): number {
    return this.#value;
  }

  public increment(): void {
    this.#value += 1;
  }
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 9. EVENT / CALLBACK NAMING
//    • on<Event> for props/callbacks, handle<Event> for internal handlers.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
interface FormProps {
  onSubmit: (data: CreateUserInput) => void;
  onError: (error: Error) => void;
}

function handleSubmit(data: CreateUserInput): void {
  console.log("submitting", data);
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// DEMO — exercise everything above
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
async function main(): Promise<void> {
  const newUser: CreateUserInput = {
    email: "ada@example.com",
    role: UserRole.ADMIN,
  };

  // simulated id
  const created: User = {
    ...newUser,
    id: crypto.randomUUID(),
    createdAt: new Date(),
  };

  await userRepository.save(created);

  const found = await getUserById(created.id);
  console.log("found:", found?.email);

  console.log("isAdult(20):", isAdult(20));
  console.log("currency:", formatCurrency(1234.5, "USD"));
  console.log("button:", SubmitButton({ label: "Save", onClick: () => {} }));

  const counter = useCounter(0);
  counter.increment();
  console.log("counter value:", counter.value);

  const doubled = mapArray([1, 2, 3], (n) => n * 2);
  console.log("doubled:", doubled);

  const c = new Counter();
  c.increment();
  console.log("counter (class) value:", c.value);
}

main().catch((err: unknown) => {
  console.error(err);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

## Quick Reference Table

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| File | `kebab-case` | `user-profile.service.ts` |
| Variable / param | `camelCase` | `userId`, `isLoading` |
| Function / method | `camelCase` (verb) | `getUserById` |
| Class / Interface / Type / Enum | `PascalCase` | `UserRepository`, `UserRole` |
| Enum member | `UPPER_SNAKE` or `PascalCase` | `UserRole.ADMIN` |
| Constant (compile-time) | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |
| React component | `PascalCase` | `SubmitButton` |
| React hook | `useCamelCase` | `useCounter` |
| Generic type param | `T`, `TItem`, `TResult` | `mapArray<TInput, TOutput>` |
| Private field | `#field` or `private` | `#value` |
| Boolean | `is/has/can/should` prefix | `isAuthenticated` |

## Notes on Disputed Conventions

- **`I` prefix on interfaces** (`IUser`): older C#-influenced style. Modern TS (and the official handbook) discourages it because interfaces and types are interchangeable-ish and the prefix adds noise.
- **`_` underscore for unused params**: use `_param` or just omit; with `noUnusedParameters` you may need the underscore. Rename bindings to `_` are common: `arr.map((_, i) => i)`.
- **Type vs Interface**: both `PascalCase`. Prefer `interface` for object shapes that may be extended; `type` for unions/intersections/mapped types.

