## 10. UDP edge cases

UDP preserves message boundaries but has size limits and can report ICMP errors as socket errors.

```ts
import dgram from 'dgram';

const sock = dgram.createSocket('udp4');

sock.on('error', (err) => {
  // ECONNREFUSED often means ICMP port unreachable
  console.error('UDP error:', err.code, err.message);
});

sock.bind(41234, () => {
  sock.setBroadcast(true);
  sock.setMulticastTTL(128);
});

sock.on('message', (msg, rinfo) => {
  // IPv4 max practical payload ~65507 bytes; larger may be truncated/fragmented
  if (msg.length > 65507) {
    console.warn('Oversized UDP datagram');
  }
  console.log(rinfo.address, rinfo.port, msg.toString());
});
```

Edge cases:
- datagram truncation
- multicast interface selection
- broadcast permissions
- no delivery guarantees

