## 12. Server accept backlog and resource exhaustion

Protect the server from slowloris and too many connections.

```ts
import net from 'net';

const server = net.createServer((socket) => {
  socket.on('error', (e) => {
    if (e.code !== 'ECONNRESET') console.error(e);
  });
});

server.maxConnections = 1000;

server.on('error', (err: NodeJS.ErrnoException) => {
  if (err.code === 'EADDRINUSE') {
    console.error('Port already in use');
    process.exit(1);
  }
  console.error(err);
});

server.listen(8080, () => {
  console.log('Listening');
});
```

Also useful:
- `ulimit -n` / file descriptor limits
- cluster mode or `SO_REUSEPORT`
- request body size limits in HTTP frameworks

