## 4. Syntax patterns you’ll see in TS math code

| Pattern | Purpose | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `readonly T[]` | Non-mutating input | `function sum(xs: readonly number[])` |
| Generics `<T extends number>` | Constrain to numeric | `function scale<T extends number>(x:T): number` |
| Rest params | Variadic math | `function max(...xs: number[])` |
| Tuple types | Fixed-size vectors | `type Vec2 = [number, number]` |
| `as const` | Literal constants | `const EPS = 1e-9 as const` |
| Overloads | Multiple call shapes | `clamp(x, lo, hi)` vs `clamp(x, range)` |
| `satisfies` (TS 4.9+) | Check without widening | `const cfg = { eps: 1e-6 } satisfies { eps: number }` |

