## 12. Testing: rollback after every test

```ts
import { beforeAll, afterAll, afterEach } from "vitest";
// pseudocode
let client: any;

beforeAll(async () => { client = await pool.connect(); });
afterEach(async () => { await client.query("ROLLBACK"); await client.query("BEGIN"); });
afterAll(async () => { await client.query("ROLLBACK"); client.release(); });

it("creates user", async () => {
  await client.query("INSERT INTO users(email) VALUES ($1)", ["t@example.com"]);
  const { rows } = await client.query("SELECT count(*) FROM users");
  expect(Number(rows[0].count)).toBe(1);
  // afterEach rolls back
});
```

For Prisma, use a transaction + rollback strategy in test setup; beware interactive transactions cannot span test hooks easily—use a savepoint-per-test or schema reset.

