### 1) Converging pointers — Two Sum II (sorted input)

```ts
function twoSumSorted(nums: number[], target: number): [number, number] | null {
  let left = 0;
  let right = nums.length - 1;

  while (left < right) {
    const sum = nums[left] + nums[right];
    if (sum === target) return [left, right];
    if (sum < target) left++;      // need larger sum
    else right--;                   // need smaller sum
  }
  return null;
}

// twoSumSorted([2, 7, 11, 15], 9) -> [0, 1]
```

**Why it works:** sorted order lets one comparison decide which pointer to move, eliminating a whole row of the search space.

