## 11. Confusing slow/fast with left/right

Using the wrong variant for the problem (e.g., cycle detection needs fast/slow, not left/right).

```ts
// ❌ Bug: left/right can't detect a cycle in a linked list
function hasCycleBad(head: ListNode | null): boolean {
  let l = head, r = head;
  while (l && r) {
    l = l.next;
    r = r?.next?.next ?? null; // r may skip null; logic inconsistent
    if (l === r) return true;
  }
  return false;
}
// Actually this IS Floyd's; the pitfall is mixing variants.

// ✅ Fix: use the right variant per problem
// - Sorted array search/sum  -> left/right
// - In-place compaction/dedup -> slow/fast (same direction)
// - Cycle detection           -> fast/slow (Floyd's)
```

