```

Notice the quoted name `Carol, Jr.`. A simple `split(",")` would break on that field, which is why a real CSV parser is used.

### Step 3: Define domain types

We separate raw CSV rows from validated domain objects. This keeps parsing and business logic clean.

```ts
interface EmployeeRaw {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  department: string;
  salary: string;
  active: string;
}

interface Employee {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  department: string;
  salary: number;
  active: boolean;
}

